 "source": {
  "prompt": "A cliffside port city climbing out of a small bay. A flat harbor of cranes and container stacks at the waterline, an entertainment strip of neon stairs and terraces on the slope above it, a corporate crown of towers on a cliff-edged plateau looking down on the bay, an old quarter of crooked streets on a hill to the west, megablocks stacked along a ridge to the east, and a river valley running down from the north. Highways tunnel through the hills; a metro runs deep under them.",
  "notes": "M13's hilly sample. Art direction: the bay on the south side so the iso camera (from the south) looks up the slopes at the crown; the crown is a plateau 30 m over the harbor with a hill on it, so its towers stand highest; the old quarter and the ridge frame it; the harbor is levelled flat. Highways stay on the ground (no viaducts): they climb in cuts and bore through the hills."
 },
